One file per feature.

A feature adds `<feature>.handler.mjs` here and touches no other file. The file's default export is

    export default { types: ["..."], channel: "ui" | "content", handle(body, ctx) }

- `types` are message types from the table of the channel (`UI_TYPES` for "ui",
  `CONTENT_TYPES` for "content") in `src/shared/protocol.mjs`.
- `handle` receives the checked body and a context that the router builds. The
  router has already checked the sender and decoded the message.

The router reads a generated register of these files. There is no central list
and no central `switch`: two features never edit the same file.
